Here is code based on the [Pattern 3 - Dueling buttons](https://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/action-buttons.html) example. 

When using purrr to create the observeEvents, I can only get normal distributions (the runif button doesn't work).

**Update: @jcheng5 correctly pointed out that this can be fixed with `force()`. He suggested I file it here in the hopes that the force isn't necessary.**

```r
library(shiny)
library(purrr)

